WEBVTT

00:00.730 --> 00:04.710
<i>Tsubasa and his friends have made their way to the National Tournament,</i>

00:04.710 --> 00:08.190
<i>but Wakabayashi's condition has taken a turn for the worse.</i>

00:08.190 --> 00:11.060
<i>He is unable to participate in the National Tournament!</i>

00:11.060 --> 00:12.680
<i>With his injury worsening as it has,</i>

00:12.680 --> 00:15.360
<i>he must remain behind, unable to play for the time being.</i>

00:15.360 --> 00:18.390
<i>Tsubasa has decided to carry on in his stead,</i>

00:18.390 --> 00:21.080
<i>promising that he'll keep winning until the finals.</i>

00:21.880 --> 00:24.240
<i>Now, with Tsubasa being selected as the new captain,</i>

00:24.240 --> 00:28.580
<i>Nankatsu FC has been reborn as a brand new team.</i>

00:28.580 --> 00:29.710
<i>And finally...</i>

00:32.210 --> 00:37.130
I pledge! We participants, will act with sportsmanship

00:37.130 --> 00:40.870
and will compete while adhering to the tenets of fair play!

00:40.870 --> 00:45.810
I am the captain of Nankatsu FC, Tsubasa Ozora!

00:46.730 --> 00:50.860
<i>The National Youth Football Tournament finally kicks off!</i>

00:51.720 --> 00:55.510
<i>As luck would have it, Nankatsu's first match will be Meiwa FC,</i>

00:55.510 --> 01:01.620
<i>another contender for the champion's title.</i>

01:02.590 --> 01:05.450
All right! This is the crucial first match.

01:05.450 --> 01:07.330
Everyone, put everything you've got into it!

01:07.330 --> 01:08.830
Yes!

01:09.390 --> 01:11.210
Nice shot! Next!

01:11.210 --> 01:12.210
Tsubasa!

01:12.560 --> 01:13.710
<i>Wakabayashi...</i>

01:14.320 --> 01:17.480
<i>I'll make sure my leg is fully healed for the next match against Meiwa.</i>

01:17.480 --> 01:20.430
<i>So, Tsubasa... I'm counting on you!</i>

01:20.430 --> 01:23.120
<i>Our first match will be against Meiwa.</i>

01:23.120 --> 01:28.310
<i>I'll score with my own two legs, and win this match in your stead!</i>

01:29.560 --> 01:31.560
Tsubasa's on fire!

01:31.560 --> 01:33.570
That's right! I'm really fired up!

01:33.570 --> 01:35.650
All right, let's do our best!

01:35.650 --> 01:37.280
Yeah!

01:37.740 --> 01:41.530
Meiwa FC's players, it's almost time. Can you please go...

01:44.950 --> 01:47.460
Coach, looks like it's time.

01:47.460 --> 01:53.090
Go ahead. My being there is unimportant.

01:53.960 --> 01:56.510
MEIWA FC COACH: KOZO KIRA

01:56.510 --> 02:01.090
That doesn't sound like something a coach should say.

02:01.090 --> 02:02.010
You're right.

02:02.010 --> 02:05.380
But he's the one who raised Hyuga and Takeshi

02:05.380 --> 02:09.140
and helped us get this far in a short amount of time.

02:09.140 --> 02:12.990
Kojiro, you're going out there to win.

02:12.990 --> 02:15.440
No one would complain if you just win, right?

02:16.330 --> 02:17.440
Yes.

02:18.590 --> 02:21.450
Now this... this is a traffic jam.

02:21.450 --> 02:25.450
I've been watching this tournament for years, but this is the first time I see something like this.

02:25.450 --> 02:29.790
Goes to show you how much attention this match is attracting.

02:30.450 --> 02:32.030
I'm looking forward to this.

02:32.030 --> 02:36.110
I wonder what possibilities these boys will show us...

02:50.080 --> 02:55.710
<i>The smell of the grass when I stumbled,</i>

02:50.080 --> 02:55.710
<i>koronda toki no shibafu no nioi</i>

02:55.710 --> 03:00.710
<i>the endless blue of the sky above...</i>

02:55.710 --> 03:00.710
<i>aogimita sora no ao hateshinakatta</i>

03:01.380 --> 03:06.550
<i>This winding, back-and-forth path</i>

03:01.380 --> 03:06.550
<i>mayotte modori susumu kidô ga</i>

03:07.260 --> 03:14.880
<i>is a map for our endless dreams</i>

03:07.260 --> 03:14.880
<i>hateshinai yume o miru boku-tachi no chizu</i>

03:14.880 --> 03:20.650
<i>Even if my hopes miss the goal</i>

03:14.880 --> 03:20.650
<i>goal o soreta kibô ga atte mo</i>

03:20.650 --> 03:29.160
<i>if I stand back up, my dreams will never end</i>

03:20.650 --> 03:29.160
<i>mata tachiagaru nara yume wa owaranai</i>

03:29.160 --> 03:34.960
<i>No.1! Race forth, faster than anyone</i>

03:29.160 --> 03:34.960
<i>No. 1! dare yori hayaku kakenuke</i>

03:34.960 --> 03:40.880
<i>Make a starting dash toward the world stage with your tricky plays!</i>

03:34.960 --> 03:40.880
<i>tricky na play de sekai e muke Start! Dash!</i>

03:40.880 --> 03:42.380
<i>Run & Run!</i>

03:42.380 --> 03:49.680
<i>Aspirations are the one buzz, buzz, buzz that gets us moving</i>

03:42.380 --> 03:49.680
<i>akogare dake ga boku-ra o chiri-chiri-chiri ugokasu yo
</i>

03:49.680 --> 03:52.600
<i>Blaze, blaze, blaze! Let's go, it's kickoff!</i>

03:49.680 --> 03:52.600
<i>mera-mera-mera iku ze kickoff</i>

03:52.600 --> 03:57.520
<i>Leap out into a giant field of dreams</i>

03:52.600 --> 03:57.520
<i>tobidasô dodekai dream field</i>

04:08.390 --> 04:13.350
<b><b>EPISODE 14:
FIRE UP, NANKATSU! DEFEAT MEIWA!!</b></b>

04:08.960 --> 04:14.190
<i>The first matches of the group stages will be simultaneously held in this venue.</i>

04:14.190 --> 04:18.510
<i>Right before the match that would raise the curtain on the tournament was about to begin,</i>

04:18.510 --> 04:21.480
<i>something unexpected was awaiting the boys.</i>

04:23.500 --> 04:31.290
<i>Almost all of the spectators had gathered where the Nankatsu vs. Meiwa match was to take place!</i>

04:31.290 --> 04:33.810
There really are a lot of spectators here...

04:33.810 --> 04:36.550
Yeah, this atmosphere almost puts Brazil to shame.

04:36.550 --> 04:39.170
There are a lot of fans who know their stuff.

04:39.170 --> 04:41.030
This is a can't-miss match!

04:41.030 --> 04:44.170
People are saying this is the real final match.

04:44.170 --> 04:47.260
Man, just look at that...

04:47.260 --> 04:50.190
Misaki! Do your best!

04:50.190 --> 04:52.310
We'll be cheering you on!

04:52.310 --> 04:54.190
Thanks, Matsuyama!

04:54.190 --> 04:56.310
You do your best too, Furano Elementary!

04:56.310 --> 04:58.730
Tsubasa, do your best!

04:58.730 --> 05:00.560
So, this match will really determine

05:01.480 --> 05:04.320
who my greatest opponent will be.

05:06.110 --> 05:09.280
Oh, Meiwa FC is finally on the field!

05:11.080 --> 05:13.160
It's been a while, Nankatsu.

05:13.690 --> 05:16.460
Kojiro Hyuga...

05:19.290 --> 05:22.920
Hey, you're the kid who made the pledge yesterday.

05:22.920 --> 05:25.760
Then let me make my pledge here and now!

05:27.420 --> 05:30.660
We'll win the National Tournament!

05:30.660 --> 05:34.850
So, the team to win this match will be ours, Meiwa FC!

05:35.980 --> 05:38.350
This bastard...

05:44.760 --> 05:48.780
<i>Players from both teams get into their respective positions.</i>

05:49.350 --> 05:54.040
<i>Shizuoka's representative, Nankatsu FC, is known for their magnificent passing.</i>

05:54.040 --> 05:55.910
<i>They're lined up in a 4-3-3.</i>

05:56.620 --> 06:01.670
<i>Their famous goalkeeper, Wakabayashi, is unfortunately unable to play due to injury.</i>

06:01.670 --> 06:04.880
<i>However, the second-string Morisaki is quite competent, himself.</i>

06:04.880 --> 06:08.390
<i>With the giant center-back player Takasugi's presence,</i>

06:08.390 --> 06:10.760
<i>their defenders will heavily protect the front area of the goal.</i>

06:10.760 --> 06:15.770
<i>In the center field, Izawa, Misaki and Urabe form a triangle.</i>

06:15.770 --> 06:21.270
<i>Finally, Taki, Kisugi and Tsubasa are in charge of Nankatsu's attack.</i>

06:21.640 --> 06:23.730
Guys, let's give it all we've got!

06:24.110 --> 06:25.520
Yeah!

06:26.320 --> 06:30.130
<i>Against them is Saitama's representative, Meiwa FC. They're set up in a 4-4-2.</i>

06:30.130 --> 06:32.480
<i>With the ferocious tiger, Kojiro Hyuga as their lead,</i>

06:32.480 --> 06:35.410
<i>they are a team that hold their opponents down through their hard work.</i>

06:35.410 --> 06:39.890
<i>The one in the attacking midfielder position is the only 4th grader in the team, Takeshi Sawada.</i>

06:39.890 --> 06:42.670
<i>What kind of play will he show us?</i>

06:43.850 --> 06:45.830
<i>The final line is entrusted to these four,</i>

06:45.830 --> 06:48.920
<i>with the goalkeeper Kawaguchi charged with protecting the goal.</i>

06:50.700 --> 06:53.640
Oh, this is a great view!

06:53.640 --> 06:56.390
I like this scenery...

06:57.640 --> 07:03.810
Well, go ahead, Kojiro. The ones who'll rule over the big stage is none other than us, Meiwa FC.

07:05.450 --> 07:12.180
<i>The first match of the tournament, Nankatsu FC vs. Meiwa FC, kicks-off among the wild cheering.</i>

07:13.230 --> 07:15.320
Like I'd lose to the likes of Meiwa!

07:15.320 --> 07:16.370
Come at me!

07:17.070 --> 07:21.410
<i>Tsubasa Ozora, Nankatsu's ace, fiercely dribbles ahead as the whistle is blown!</i>

07:21.410 --> 07:27.130
<i>Kojiro Hyuga, Meiwa's ace, comes forward to meet him!</i>

07:32.040 --> 07:34.550
<i>Both aces clash right at the beginning!</i>

07:36.050 --> 07:38.780
<i>Their duel results in a draw!</i>

07:38.780 --> 07:41.060
<i>The ball flies high up in the sky!</i>

07:41.060 --> 07:42.180
This bastard...

07:45.280 --> 07:46.110
Here!

07:46.110 --> 07:47.110
All right!

07:47.110 --> 07:49.110
Damn it!

07:51.510 --> 07:53.200
<i>My leg!</i>

07:53.200 --> 07:55.700
<i>My leg is numb from that clash...!</i>

08:00.370 --> 08:03.080
<i>The pillar of the team, Hyuga can't chase them!</i>

08:03.080 --> 08:05.710
<i>Is this Nankatsu's first chance for a goal?</i>

08:06.110 --> 08:07.250
I'm counting on you!

08:07.250 --> 08:09.040
All right, I've got this!

08:09.940 --> 08:12.050
<i>Denied! Meiwa manages to cut through this attack!</i>

08:12.050 --> 08:15.800
<i>The one who pulls it off is the 4th grader everyone's talking about, Takeshi Sawada!</i>

08:15.800 --> 08:17.970
<i>He shows off his sharp senses right off the bat.</i>

08:17.970 --> 08:18.930
Damn it!

08:18.930 --> 08:20.100
Takeshi...

08:21.680 --> 08:22.730
This guy!

08:23.290 --> 08:24.480
What?

08:27.340 --> 08:27.990
Oh no!

08:27.990 --> 08:29.120
<i>It's a one-two!</i>

08:29.120 --> 08:32.040
<i>You wouldn't expect Sawada to be a 4th grader with this kind of ball control.</i>

08:32.040 --> 08:35.400
<i>The tables have turned! Is it now Meiwa's first chance at a goal?</i>

08:35.400 --> 08:38.170
Looks like my leg's better, now!

08:38.170 --> 08:39.740
All right, let's do this, Takeshi!

08:39.740 --> 08:43.750
Sawada meets up with Hyuga in front of the goal.

08:44.410 --> 08:45.930
Takeshi...

08:45.930 --> 08:47.830
You've really improved.

08:47.830 --> 08:50.420
Misaki! Thanks!

08:50.420 --> 08:54.090
Coach Kira trained me a lot as well.

08:55.000 --> 08:57.340
<i>Is he talking about that guy who taught Kojiro?</i>

08:57.340 --> 08:59.720
Misaki, I'm going to have to ask you to let me through!

09:00.220 --> 09:02.690
<i>Misaki lets the ball through his legs...!</i>

09:02.690 --> 09:03.720
I did it!

09:05.220 --> 09:06.810
<i>No, he won't let him through!</i>

09:07.480 --> 09:08.770
Nice, Misaki!

09:08.770 --> 09:11.320
<i>His opponents can't do anything against Misaki's technical play!</i>

09:11.320 --> 09:13.230
<i>Just as I expected from Misaki...</i>

09:13.230 --> 09:17.740
That damn Misaki... If I'd gotten that ball, I was sure to score...!

09:27.650 --> 09:31.990
Excuse me! Can you tell me the current score of Nankatsu's match?

09:31.990 --> 09:34.560
<i>Misaki's speed is amazing!</i>

09:34.560 --> 09:36.510
<i>His swiftness down the pitch lives up to its reputation!</i>

09:36.510 --> 09:37.300
Damn it!

09:37.300 --> 09:38.680
Stop him quickly!

09:42.520 --> 09:45.220
<i>Misaki changes the pace with a long pass!</i>

09:45.920 --> 09:48.730
<i>It reaches Tsubasa as he broke off into a run to the area!</i>

09:48.730 --> 09:50.290
<i>As expected of Misaki!</i>

09:50.290 --> 09:53.070
<i>He didn't let Meiwa's defense get in his way!</i>

09:53.930 --> 09:54.530
All right!

09:57.360 --> 10:02.580
<i>What?! Tsubasa changes direction, making a dash for facing Hyuga head on!</i>

10:02.580 --> 10:05.450
<i>Why? That was his chance for a fast break!</i>

10:05.450 --> 10:08.330
Is this runt seriously planning to get past me, no matter what?!

10:08.670 --> 10:10.090
Don't give me that crap!

10:10.090 --> 10:12.540
I'll steal the ball!

10:14.240 --> 10:17.010
<i>What the—? The ball has disappeared!</i>

10:18.220 --> 10:20.380
<i>T-this is...</i>

10:20.380 --> 10:21.890
It's a heel lift!

10:24.280 --> 10:30.480
<i>What was that from Tsubasa? He flicked the ball with his heel, lifting it over Hyuga!</i>

10:30.480 --> 10:33.440
<i>And as the ball floats down to his feet...</i>

10:35.440 --> 10:37.780
<i>He fires off a volley!</i>

10:48.080 --> 10:50.790
You did it, Tsubasa!

10:51.630 --> 10:53.540
<i>He scored!</i>

10:53.540 --> 10:56.920
<i>In the third minute of the first half, Nankatsu takes the lead with Tsubasa's shot!</i>

10:57.720 --> 11:00.800
The one who'll win isn't Meiwa, it's Nankatsu!

11:02.430 --> 11:04.560
<i>That was quite the surprise!</i>

11:04.560 --> 11:07.390
<i>Even though he's the center-forward of Nankatsu, a favorite for the champion's title,</i>

11:07.390 --> 11:11.850
<i>Tsubasa Ozora, a no-name player at the national level, has managed to open the score</i>

11:11.850 --> 11:15.900
<i>against the powerhouse Meiwa FC right at the start of the game!</i>

11:15.900 --> 11:21.900
What do you mean "no-name"? Tsubasa scored a hat-trick in every match in the prefectural tournament!

11:21.900 --> 11:25.200
<i>That's a really high-level technique.</i>

11:25.200 --> 11:27.660
<i>Is this really an elementary school student's play?</i>

11:27.660 --> 11:29.080
One, two...

11:29.080 --> 11:33.000
Way to go, Nankatsu!

11:33.000 --> 11:37.750
All right, if this is how it's going to be, I'll cheer for Nankatsu too!

11:38.570 --> 11:43.050
<i>Hyuga was challenged and defeated by Tsubasa.</i>

11:43.050 --> 11:45.340
<i>Given his aggressive disposition,</i>

11:45.340 --> 11:48.260
<i>he must be burning with rage inside!</i>

11:48.640 --> 11:53.730
<i>Kojiro, when you came to scout us out, you forgot about one piece of information.</i>

11:54.340 --> 11:59.190
<i>We don't only have Wakabayashi. We also have Tsubasa.</i>

11:59.190 --> 12:04.700
I'm sorry, Hyuga. This happened because I let Misaki steal the ball from me.

12:06.570 --> 12:08.330
Hyuga...

12:15.040 --> 12:18.150
<i>That's it, I like those eyes.</i>

12:18.150 --> 12:24.080
<i>As long as that look doesn't leave your eyes, you won't ever lose, Kojiro.</i>

12:36.750 --> 12:39.770
<i>The match resumes with Meiwa's kick-off.</i>

12:41.820 --> 12:44.570
<i>Nankatsu steals the ball immediately!</i>

12:44.570 --> 12:46.770
Way to go, Nankatsu!

12:46.770 --> 12:49.910
<i>After Tsubasa's first goal, they are in top condition!</i>

12:49.910 --> 12:52.290
Go, let's get another one!

12:53.060 --> 12:53.830
Crap!

12:54.590 --> 12:55.500
Hyuga!

12:55.500 --> 12:57.430
<i>What's wrong with Hyuga?</i>

12:57.430 --> 13:00.460
<i>He's been waiting next to the goal since then.</i>

13:03.460 --> 13:04.720
Eat this!

13:04.720 --> 13:07.590
<i>The keeper barely grazes it!</i>

13:07.590 --> 13:09.140
<i>Is this their second one?</i>

13:09.140 --> 13:10.560
<i>No, it hits the post!</i>

13:10.560 --> 13:11.140
Damn!

13:11.140 --> 13:12.890
<i>Hyuga's still not moving!</i>

13:14.640 --> 13:17.020
<i>Sawada recovers the ball and clears it!</i>

13:18.110 --> 13:18.850
All right!

13:18.850 --> 13:21.360
<i>The clear is intercepted by Tsubasa!</i>

13:21.360 --> 13:23.360
Go, Tsubasa!

13:23.360 --> 13:25.300
We're counting on you for another one!

13:25.300 --> 13:26.860
Tsubasa!

13:26.860 --> 13:28.740
<i>Meiwa is being kept on defense!</i>

13:28.740 --> 13:30.970
<i>Hyuga is eerily silent!</i>

13:30.970 --> 13:32.280
<i>What is going on?!</i>

13:32.280 --> 13:35.290
Hyuga, he comes! Tsubasa Ozora!

13:36.500 --> 13:39.130
Don't get full of yourself!

13:39.130 --> 13:42.240
<i>Hyuga was being motionless, but has sprung to life as soon</i>

13:42.240 --> 13:46.260
<i>as the ball went to Tsubasa, fiercely dashing forward!</i>

13:46.260 --> 13:49.760
<i>This is a completely different situation from the first goal!</i>

13:50.280 --> 13:53.010
<i>Now it's Hyuga who is challenging Tsubasa, one-on-one!</i>

13:53.790 --> 13:55.680
I won't lose!

13:56.040 --> 13:57.560
Eat this!

13:58.190 --> 14:02.360
<i>Wow, this is Hyuga's sliding— no, it's a diving tackle!</i>

14:04.240 --> 14:06.420
<i>Tsubasa can't get around in time!</i>

14:06.420 --> 14:07.900
<i>Hyuga is faster!</i>

14:10.200 --> 14:12.410
Tsubasa!

14:13.580 --> 14:15.410
<i>Tsubasa is sent flying!</i>

14:15.900 --> 14:19.080
<i>Since he's won the ball, there's no whistle; play will continue!</i>

14:19.080 --> 14:24.590
<i>What a tenacious, hard play from Hyuga!</i>

14:24.590 --> 14:27.340
<i>So, Nankatsu will be the champion, you say?</i>

14:27.340 --> 14:28.040
Damn!

14:28.040 --> 14:30.800
How dare you do that to Tsubasa! I'll stop you here!

14:30.800 --> 14:32.340
Don't make me laugh!

14:32.720 --> 14:34.970
<i>Hyuga gets ready to shoot!</i>

14:34.970 --> 14:36.560
He's shooting from way back there?!

14:36.560 --> 14:38.430
Let's block him together!

14:39.310 --> 14:45.950
We, Meiwa will be the champions!

14:48.820 --> 14:50.560
What, the ball is—

14:50.560 --> 14:51.820
it's gone!

14:51.820 --> 14:53.820
CAN I JUST GET A CRUNCH SOUND EFFECT HERE LIKE I WANT DEAF PEOPLE TO KNOW THIS MAN'S LIFE IS RUINED

14:58.030 --> 15:00.310
<i>He scored!</i>

15:00.310 --> 15:03.290
<i>An incredible shot that sends the keeper flying!</i>

15:09.050 --> 15:11.050
You did it, Hyuga!

15:11.480 --> 15:13.970
Awesome... what a powerful shot.

15:13.970 --> 15:17.670
<i>That's Hyuga's true strength...!</i>

15:17.670 --> 15:20.810
<i>10 minutes into the first half, Meiwa has caught up!</i>

15:20.810 --> 15:24.230
<i>The frightening ferocious tiger, Kojiro Hyuga!</i>

15:24.230 --> 15:27.960
That boy... he deliberately aimed for the keeper's face.

15:27.960 --> 15:29.240
But... why?

15:29.240 --> 15:32.740
Yes, that's it Kojiro.

15:32.740 --> 15:34.740
Are you all right, Morisaki?

15:35.500 --> 15:37.240
Sc— Scary...

15:38.680 --> 15:40.790
<i>Kojiro Hyuga...</i>

15:40.790 --> 15:44.580
<i>The match between Nankatsu and Meiwa is now at an even score, 1-1!</i>

15:44.580 --> 15:47.710
It's a one-on-one battle between Kojiro and Tsubasa.

15:53.940 --> 15:55.720
Finesse versus power.

15:55.720 --> 15:56.690
Huh?

15:56.690 --> 15:59.790
I mean, if we say Tsubasa is a striker with finesse,

15:59.790 --> 16:02.590
then Hyuga is the one with the power.

16:02.590 --> 16:03.480
I see.

16:03.900 --> 16:05.980
That's not all though.

16:06.430 --> 16:09.710
Tsubasa loves football from the bottom of his heart and

16:09.710 --> 16:13.150
it feels like the ball is an extension of him.

16:13.150 --> 16:17.110
Compared to that, Hyuga plays football with ferocity.

16:17.110 --> 16:20.740
It feels as if he channels all his fighting spirit to the ball.

16:20.740 --> 16:22.160
Exactly.

16:22.160 --> 16:26.300
The teachers behind their football also stand in stark contrast to each other.

16:26.300 --> 16:30.320
I know... former Brazil representative, Roberto Hongo,

16:30.320 --> 16:32.970
and Meiwa's coach, Kozo Kira.

16:33.550 --> 16:39.110
A mysterious talent who left the football world without paying any attention to

16:39.110 --> 16:43.700
scouts from overseas, back when there wasn't a professional league in Japan.

16:43.700 --> 16:46.190
The more you compare the two, the more interesting it gets.

16:47.230 --> 16:50.940
But... one ace striker is enough.

16:50.940 --> 16:55.990
If we continue to watch, we will have our answer as to which one we should need in the end.

16:57.360 --> 16:59.350
<i>Nankatsu has conceded a goal, and the score is even.</i>

16:59.350 --> 17:00.990
<i>It's time for the counterattack</i>

17:00.990 --> 17:02.210
Don't lose Misaki!

17:02.210 --> 17:03.250
Do your best!

17:03.250 --> 17:04.460
All right!

17:04.460 --> 17:07.040
<i>The young Sawada is approaching to get the ball.</i>

17:07.040 --> 17:09.750
<i>Misaki dodges him, showing off his excellent ball handling!</i>

17:10.250 --> 17:12.420
<i>He is on the next level when it comes to this.</i>

17:12.420 --> 17:13.220
Hey!

17:14.080 --> 17:16.180
<i>Misaki makes a brilliant heel pass!</i>

17:16.180 --> 17:17.100
Take it!

17:17.100 --> 17:19.720
<i>And Kisugi connects the ball with one touch!</i>

17:20.390 --> 17:21.680
All right, the ball makes it through to Tsubasa!

17:21.680 --> 17:24.430
<i>Tsubasa advances with the ball!</i>

17:25.430 --> 17:28.170
Okay, all of you defenders, mark Tsubasa with all you've got!

17:28.170 --> 17:30.610
Now is the time to show the results of your special training!

17:30.610 --> 17:32.070
Yeah!

17:33.470 --> 17:38.360
<i>All of Meiwa's defenders charge at Tsubasa after Hyuga's command!</i>

17:38.360 --> 17:40.240
Take this!

17:41.370 --> 17:43.790
<i>Now that's a rain of sliding tackles!</i>

17:43.790 --> 17:46.120
<i>Tsubasa dodges them with his utmost efforts!</i>

17:48.680 --> 17:50.100
Woah, what did he just—!

17:50.100 --> 17:51.810
He didn't just slide,

17:51.810 --> 17:54.210
but pivoted with his hand to go for another!

17:55.050 --> 17:56.800
<i>Tsubasa is in a dangerous situation!</i>

17:57.560 --> 17:59.800
<i>Dodged by a hair's breadth!</i>

18:01.260 --> 18:05.770
<i>From Tsubasa's behind, one of Meiwa's players slams into his leg!</i>

18:05.770 --> 18:07.390
Oh, Tsubasa!

18:08.270 --> 18:09.920
<i>Tsubasa is on the ground!</i>

18:09.920 --> 18:11.650
<i>Of course this was a foul play.</i>

18:11.650 --> 18:13.150
<i>Yellow card!</i>

18:13.150 --> 18:17.350
That's right. If I'm against an opponent that I can't stop no matter what I do,

18:17.350 --> 18:19.910
I just have to stop him even if I have to go against the rules!

18:19.910 --> 18:20.980
Yes!

18:20.980 --> 18:21.910
Damn it!

18:21.910 --> 18:26.410
I'll show you the difference between our skills from now on.

18:26.850 --> 18:29.500
<i>Nankatsu gets a free kick after the foul.</i>

18:29.500 --> 18:31.110
<i>He's underestimating us.</i>

18:31.110 --> 18:32.710
<i>I'll take Tsubasa's revenge!</i>

18:34.450 --> 18:37.130
<i>Hyuga blocks it easily!</i>

18:37.130 --> 18:41.300
<i>Oh, Tsubasa runs at Hyuga!</i>

18:41.300 --> 18:43.170
<i>What a stubborn guy...</i>

18:43.170 --> 18:47.610
<i>With every goal we score, we seem to be on equal terms in the challenge.</i>

18:48.190 --> 18:49.530
<i>However, you're dead wrong.</i>

18:49.530 --> 18:51.650
<i>And I'll prove it to you, right now!</i>

18:51.650 --> 18:53.210
Take this!

18:53.210 --> 18:55.610
<i>What! Hyuga passed the ball!</i>

18:56.560 --> 18:59.320
All right! Shoot, Takeshi!

19:00.320 --> 19:01.820
Okay!

19:02.600 --> 19:05.830
<i>Sawada fires a reckless long shot!</i>

19:06.290 --> 19:09.790
What is this? Anyone can stop a shot like this one.

19:11.120 --> 19:12.040
What?

19:12.040 --> 19:14.660
<i>What happened just now?</i>

19:14.660 --> 19:16.800
<i>Goalkeeper Morisaki couldn't even move a finger!</i>

19:16.800 --> 19:19.720
I'm... I'm scared of the ball...

19:20.550 --> 19:26.060
Did Kojiro hit Morisaki on the chin to make him scared of the ball?!

19:26.060 --> 19:29.390
Do you want to win so bad, Kojiro Hyuga?!

19:29.390 --> 19:32.220
<i>Will Morisaki be unable to continue?</i>

19:32.220 --> 19:36.650
<i>If that happens, Nankatsu, who only have one goalkeeper available, will be in serious trouble!</i>

19:36.650 --> 19:38.900
As expected of Hyuga.

19:38.900 --> 19:42.660
Yeah, I'm really glad that I'm not playing against him.

19:42.660 --> 19:45.800
<i>2-1! Meiwa has finally turned the tables in their favor.</i>

19:45.800 --> 19:49.160
<i>The match resumes with Nankatsu's kick-off again.</i>

19:50.080 --> 19:51.380
<i>A hard clash!</i>

19:51.380 --> 19:52.670
<i>This is Meiwa FC's ferocious tiger!</i>

19:52.670 --> 19:55.870
All right! Keep shooting whenever you get the chance!

19:55.870 --> 19:57.920
We can get as many goals as we want against that goalkeeper!

19:57.920 --> 19:58.670
Yeah!

19:58.670 --> 19:59.670
Damn it!

20:01.170 --> 20:05.930
<i>Since their goalkeeper is acting bizarrely, Nankatsu needs to stifle those passes as soon as possible!</i>

20:06.360 --> 20:07.560
Take that!

20:07.560 --> 20:08.730
Get it, Morisaki!

20:08.730 --> 20:09.430
You can get it!

20:09.710 --> 20:11.430
<i>Will this be the third goal for Meiwa?</i>

20:12.090 --> 20:13.430
<i>No, it won't go in!</i>

20:13.430 --> 20:16.310
<i>The center forward Tsubasa came back to block!</i>

20:16.310 --> 20:17.690
Nice cover, Tsubasa!

20:17.690 --> 20:18.940
Did you see that, Meiwa?!

20:18.940 --> 20:22.450
Tsubasa played center-back in the inter-school tournament, you know?!

20:23.660 --> 20:25.360
Morisaki...

20:25.360 --> 20:27.870
The ball is your friend! Don't be afraid!

20:28.190 --> 20:29.120
What?

20:29.120 --> 20:31.120
Damn that little runt!

20:31.860 --> 20:32.620
Oh, crap!

20:33.290 --> 20:35.620
What's with this, "the ball is your friend" garbage?!

20:35.620 --> 20:38.840
If that's the case, then take this ball, too!

20:40.260 --> 20:40.760
Tsubasa, watch out!

20:40.760 --> 20:41.630
Tsubasa!

20:42.160 --> 20:44.630
<i>He gets hit right in the face!</i>

20:44.630 --> 20:48.470
If the ball is your friend, get in the goal together with your precious friend.

20:49.140 --> 20:50.060
What?

20:50.060 --> 20:55.060
<i>Tsubasa blocks the ball from entering the goal with all his body.</i>

20:56.820 --> 20:58.440
Tsubasa?

21:00.730 --> 21:03.110
See, it's fine.

21:03.790 --> 21:04.950
Tsubasa...

21:08.650 --> 21:12.660
I get it... I get it now, Tsubasa!

21:13.240 --> 21:15.140
I won't be afraid anymore.

21:15.140 --> 21:16.390
I'll give it a try.

21:16.390 --> 21:17.500
Yes.

21:17.500 --> 21:20.170
All right, that's the spirit, Morisaki!

21:20.170 --> 21:24.200
<i>Thanks to Tsubasa's amazing play, Nankatsu has overcome many critical situations, time and time again.</i>

21:24.200 --> 21:26.840
<i>However, Meiwa keeps on attacking!</i>

21:26.840 --> 21:28.720
Take this! Once more!

21:28.720 --> 21:29.720
Morisaki!

21:29.720 --> 21:30.550
All right!

21:31.600 --> 21:33.310
Morisaki, nice catch!

21:33.920 --> 21:34.560
Yeah!

21:35.190 --> 21:37.970
The football is my precious friend.

21:37.970 --> 21:39.830
Like I'd ever let it go!

21:39.830 --> 21:41.360
Isn't that right, Tsubasa?

21:41.710 --> 21:42.730
Yup!

21:42.730 --> 21:44.860
Damn that runt!

21:44.860 --> 21:47.990
He got that goalkeeper back on his feet again!

21:47.990 --> 21:51.240
Hyuga shot that ball while aiming for the goalkeeper's face.

21:51.240 --> 21:54.840
Then Tsubasa got hit on the face on purpose and stopped him.

21:54.840 --> 21:56.160
Does that mean...

21:56.160 --> 22:01.250
Yes, it does. In order to get their goalkeeper back in the game, he did it on purpose.

22:02.930 --> 22:08.350
<i>Tsubasa, I'm really glad that you're on our side and our captain.</i>

22:09.640 --> 22:11.200
<i>It's time to counter, Tsubasa!</i>

22:11.200 --> 22:13.010
<i>I'm entrusting my friend to you!</i>

22:13.560 --> 22:16.940
<i>All right! This time, it's our turn to attack!</i>

22:38.850 --> 22:44.730
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.850 --> 22:44.730
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.730 --> 22:50.740
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.730 --> 22:50.740
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.740 --> 22:56.750
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.740 --> 22:56.750
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.750 --> 23:02.210
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.750 --> 23:02.210
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.170 --> 23:08.340
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.170 --> 23:08.340
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.260 --> 23:15.060
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.260 --> 23:15.060
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.060 --> 23:21.100
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.100 --> 23:26.110
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.100 --> 23:26.110
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.400 --> 23:33.280
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.400 --> 23:33.280
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.280 --> 23:39.160
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.160 --> 23:46.050
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.160 --> 23:46.050
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:50.110 --> 24:00.640
COMING UP, EPISODE 15:
I WON'T LOSE, BECAUSE IT'S MY DREAM!
